   "name": "B",
   "overlays": [],
   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `star INDEX` and made `list` show a `*` before starred notes. The project checks pass: 3 tests OK and no lines over 100 characters.\n\nI also ran the CLI by hand. `add`, `star 0` and `list` worked, and `list` printed `*` before the starred note. `star 5` on a one-note store printed `no note at index 5`, which is the exit code 1 shown above.\n\n- **Storage:** `star(index)` in `fieldnotes/store.py` sets `\"starred\": true` on that note. It raises `IndexError` if the index is out of range. Notes saved before this change still work, since a missing `starred` field counts as not starred.\n- **CLI:** `star INDEX` in `fieldnotes/cli.py` prints `starred: <text>` on success. An out-of-range index exits 1, and a non-integer index exits 2. I also moved the usage string into one shared constant that now mentions `star`.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests, one for starring and one for an out-of-range index.\n- **Check setup:** `tools/check.py` needs the `NOTES_HOME` environment variable set. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a temporary directory.\n\nI didn't update the README.",
